---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';

export const prerender = true;
const title = 'Supported sources — extractor.sh docs';
const description = 'Supported public webpage, commerce, social, audio, podcast, and video URL formats for the extractor.sh API.';
---

<DocsLayout {title} {description} path="/docs/sources/">
  <p class="!mt-0 font-mono text-[0.78rem] font-extrabold uppercase tracking-[0.14em]">Supported sources</p>
  <h1>Paste the public page URL.</h1>
  <p class="text-[1.08rem]">Use the same address a person would open in a browser. extractor.sh recognizes the source and returns one consistent response shape.</p>

  <h2>Web pages</h2>
  <p>Public HTTP and HTTPS articles, documentation, blogs, product pages, product listings, and other content pages.</p>
  <pre><code>https://example.com/article</code></pre>
  <p>Submit the ordinary public page URL. Supported commerce pages can return a product entity with variants and specifications or a feed of repeated product cards, while other pages retain normal document and article extraction.</p>

  <h2>Amazon</h2>
  <p>Public product detail pages return one product entity. Public search results, storefronts, Idea Lists, and shared Wish Lists return product feeds.</p>
  <pre><code>https://www.amazon.de/product-name/dp/B09B8X9RGM
https://www.amazon.de/s?k=mechanical+keyboard
https://www.amazon.de/hz/wishlist/ls/EXAMPLE</code></pre>
  <p>Submit the ordinary product, search, storefront, or explicitly shared list URL. Results can include prices, ratings, review counts, seller, category, variants, specifications, and multiple images when present. List discovery, category browsing, pagination, carts, accounts, reviews, and personalized offers are unavailable. Results may be cached for up to one hour.</p>

  <h2>Apple App Store</h2>
  <p>Public app detail pages return one software product entity with the numeric App Store ID, app name, developer, description, price, ratings, version, release details, icon, and screenshots when available.</p>
  <pre><code>https://apps.apple.com/us/app/chatgpt/id6448311069</code></pre>
  <p>Submit the ordinary <code>apps.apple.com</code> page URL. Search, charts, reviews, account data, and app downloads are unavailable. Country restrictions and one-hour caching can affect current price and availability.</p>

  <h2>Bluesky</h2>
  <p>Public Bluesky profile pages return a profile entity with recent public post items. Individual post pages return one post entity.</p>
  <pre><code>https://bsky.app/profile/bsky.app
https://bsky.app/profile/bsky.app/post/3mqcp5qjdfs26</code></pre>
  <p>Replies and parent threads are not included. Profile feeds may omit complete embedded and quoted content.</p>

  <h2>Google News</h2>
  <p>Public Google News search, topic, and top-stories pages return a feed containing up to 50 article entities.</p>
  <pre><code>https://news.google.com/search?q=Cloudflare&amp;hl=en-US&amp;gl=US&amp;ceid=US%3Aen</code></pre>
  <p>Submit the ordinary Google News page URL. Results include article titles, publishers, publication dates, summaries, and source links when available. Full publisher article bodies, personalized For You results, Google Search, and Google Shopping are not included.</p>

  <h2>Google Play</h2>
  <p>Public app detail pages return one software product entity with the Android package ID, app name, developer, description, price, rating, category, content rating, icon, and screenshots when available.</p>
  <pre><code>https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.openai.chatgpt</code></pre>
  <p>Submit the ordinary Google Play app page URL. Search, category browsing, reviews, account data, and APK downloads are unavailable. Country restrictions and one-hour caching can affect current price and availability.</p>

  <h2>Instagram</h2>
  <p>Public post and reel pages can include complete exposed carousels, dimensions, coauthors, location, partnership state, and engagement. Public profile pages can include verification, pronouns, an avatar, counts, and recent public post items.</p>
  <pre><code>https://www.instagram.com/instagram/
https://www.instagram.com/p/DbbY9pdm6Q2/</code></pre>
  <p>Private or login-only content, stories, comments, transcripts, and media downloads are not supported.</p>

  <h2>Mastodon</h2>
  <p>Public status URLs on compatible Mastodon instances return one post entity containing the author, date, content warning, media descriptions, and source link when available.</p>
  <pre><code>https://mastodon.social/@trwnh/99664077509711321</code></pre>
  <p>Private statuses, timelines, complete threads, replies, and media downloads are not supported.</p>

  <h2>Shopify</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Public storefront product pages</li>
    <li>Public collection pages</li>
    <li>Public storefront homepages</li>
  </ul>
  <pre><code>https://store.example/products/black-shirt</code></pre>
  <p>Submit the ordinary public storefront page. Product pages return one product entity. Storefront and collection pages return up to 50 product entities as a feed. Protected or unavailable storefront data may produce an incomplete result or an error.</p>

  <h2><a href="/woocommerce/">WooCommerce</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Public product pages</li>
    <li>Public shop and storefront pages</li>
    <li>Public product-search result pages</li>
    <li>Public product-category pages when the store exposes a category identifier</li>
  </ul>
  <pre><code>https://store.example/product/blue-shirt/
https://store.example/?s=blue+shirt&amp;post_type=product</code></pre>
  <p>Submit the ordinary storefront URL through <code>/api/extract</code>. Product pages return one product entity, while supported shops and searches return up to 50 product entities. Results can include integer minor-unit prices, availability, ratings, categories, brands, attributes, and images.</p>

  <h2>SoundCloud</h2>
  <p>Public tracks, playlists, and sets return an audio entity. Creator pages return a profile entity.</p>
  <pre><code>https://soundcloud.com/forss/flickermood</code></pre>
  <p>Comments, waveforms, transcripts, audio analysis, and media downloads are not provided.</p>

  <h2>Spotify</h2>
  <p>Public tracks, albums, playlists, podcast shows, and episodes return an audio entity. Artist pages return a profile entity.</p>
  <pre><code>https://open.spotify.com/episode/7makk4oTQel546B0PZlDM5</code></pre>
  <p>Lyrics, transcripts, playback data, audio analysis, and media downloads are not provided.</p>

  <h2>Reddit</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Public post pages</li>
    <li>Public subreddit and community pages</li>
    <li>Public user profile pages</li>
  </ul>
  <pre><code>https://www.reddit.com/r/CloudFlare/</code></pre>
  <p>Private and quarantined communities are not supported. Post results do not include the complete comment tree.</p>

  <h2>X</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Public <code>x.com</code> status URLs</li>
    <li>Legacy <code>twitter.com</code> status URLs</li>
  </ul>
  <pre><code>https://x.com/jack/status/20</code></pre>
  <p>Private, deleted, and age-gated posts are not supported.</p>

  <h2>Yahoo Finance</h2>
  <p>Public quote and price-history pages submitted to the generic extractor return one market document with listing-currency quote values and up to one month of daily OHLCV history. For configurable history, use the provider-neutral <a href="/docs/finance/">finance endpoint</a>.</p>
  <pre><code>https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/AAPL/
https://finance.yahoo.com/quote/MSFT/history/</code></pre>
  <p>Submit the ordinary Yahoo Finance page URL. Market data can be delayed, incomplete, adjusted, or unavailable for some symbols. Results are cached for five minutes. The service does not provide live streams, order books, portfolios, trades, or investment recommendations; verify important values at the source.</p>

  <h2>TikTok</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Public video and photo post pages</li>
    <li>Public creator profile pages</li>
    <li>Short links that resolve to a supported public page</li>
  </ul>
  <pre><code>https://www.tiktok.com/@scout2015/video/6718335390845095173</code></pre>
  <p>Private, deleted, or age-restricted content, comments, transcripts, and media downloads are not supported.</p>

  <h2>Vimeo</h2>
  <p>Public Vimeo video URLs, including supported channel, group, showcase, and On Demand links, return one video entity.</p>
  <pre><code>https://vimeo.com/286898202</code></pre>
  <p>Private or embed-disabled videos, transcripts, captions, comments, and media downloads are not provided.</p>

  <h2>YouTube</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Public watch, Shorts, and <code>youtu.be</code> video pages</li>
    <li>Public channel and handle pages</li>
    <li>Public playlist pages</li>
  </ul>
  <pre><code>https://www.youtube.com/@Cloudflare</code></pre>
  <p>Video results contain public metadata, not transcripts, captions, spoken content, or media downloads.</p>
</DocsLayout>
